--- frontend/src/renderer/components/chat/ChatComposer.tsx:2444 ---
👮 **Wachiman** · 🟡❓ **Consider · question: Is attaching meant to stay closed when the message being sent has its own files? (confidence low)**

The PR body says the composer takes next-message files "only when the message being sent has no files of its own" and that attaching stays closed otherwise, as on `main`. `acceptsFiles()` and `attachBlocked` (line 956) never check `durableDelivery?.draft?.attachments`. They open on `optimisticSend` alone. Lines 929-931 instead filter the sent ids out of the strip, so the code appears to allow sent and next files in the box together. After acceptance, `clearAcceptedChatComposer` keeps `composer.attachments` unfiltered when `delivery.draft` is set (`chat-drafts.ts:1665-1667`). Can a file added during a send that has its own files be dropped or sent twice? If the body is right, add the guard. If the mix is intended, update the body and add a test.

